At Fri, 24 Feb 2006 19:49:43 +0100,
Clemens Ladisch wrote:
> 
> Takashi Iwai wrote:
> > William Nagel wrote:
> > > Unfortunately, once the device has been unplugged, snd_pcm_close()  
> > > returns an "Inappropriate ioctl for device" error, but resources are  
> > > apparently still held for the device because I don't get a new device  
> > > event if the USB device is plugged back in until my application exits.
> > 
> > Hm, it should be a bug.  snd_pcm_close() is supposed to work even in
> > the disconnected status (otherwise what could you do?)
> > 
> > Please try strace to see what ioctl fails.
> 
> Every ioctl fails in the disconnected state.  None of the
> snd_xxx_close() functions should fail to release resources.
> 
> It seems snd_ctl_close() is the only one that gets it right.
> 
> I'll fix them over the weekend if nobody else does.

Thanks :)

> BTW: I think it may be a good idea to return -ENODEV when in the
> disconnected state.  This would require a bunch of dummy functions for
> snd_shutdown_f_ops.

Sounds good to me.


Takashi


